qrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}=2{x}^{1/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & =3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2})}^{2/3} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{3C}{2}.$" 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350880 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1069 "q-8308" 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y$  that satisfies $y(0)=1.$" 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1072 #uuid "4c64ef55-bd01-5eed-b990-f133790399ab" 13194139533430 17592186045585 true] [17592186351486 1074 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x+C}\\, \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{x+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant